{"title":"2008 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 23","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A rectangular floor measures <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> feet, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> are positive integers and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/8/18850c5a6f67139956c8c1e35094c0a864ecb8ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b &gt; a$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"41\" height=\"13\" />. An artist paints a rectangle on the floor with the sides of the rectangle parallel to the floor. The unpainted part of the floor forms a border of width <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> foot around the painted rectangle and occupies half the area of the whole floor. How many possibilities are there for the ordered pair <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/8/8e8da0aef2d19017da7471378386d61620f288f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a,b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/5/9959d47fffb760b6cf89894df252b99436e4d8f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 1\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 2\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 3\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 4\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"351\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Because the unpainted part of the floor covers half the area, then the painted rectangle covers half the area as well. Since the border width is 1 foot, the dimensions of the rectangle are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/c/61c1dd3bbde066f5334db006cebf1c06cbe03807.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a-2$\" width=\"40\" height=\"12\" /> by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/2/ac2315e2ea63caf8a4b7e55c1363c55715803472.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b-2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"41\" height=\"16\" />. With this information we can make the equation:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/d/acd3a3c5ea6b851c03f4fa5f8bda9a411a904fdd.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{eqnarray*} ab &amp;=&amp; 2\\left((a-2)(b-2)\\right) \\\\ ab &amp;=&amp; 2ab - 4a - 4b + 8 \\\\ ab - 4a - 4b + 8 &amp;=&amp; 0  \\end{eqnarray*}\" width=\"313\" height=\"65\" />\nApplying <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Simon%27s_Favorite_Factoring_Trick\" title=\"Simon&#39;s Favorite Factoring Trick\">Simon's Favorite Factoring Trick</a>, we get\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/f/9df47b9e32588f9cfce3dacd23da7cc9313c8656.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{eqnarray*}ab - 4a - 4b + 16 &amp;=&amp; 8 \\\\ (a-4)(b-4) &amp;=&amp; 8 \\end{eqnarray*}\" width=\"193\" height=\"42\" />\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/8/18850c5a6f67139956c8c1e35094c0a864ecb8ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b &gt; a$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"41\" height=\"13\" />, then we have the possibilities <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/8/ea813496bc0f9d776e2bd90ef65031e7b94a2ea5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a-4) = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"87\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/4/e648a0aedd5dc11b2257e49d85ed937685dde4bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(b-4) = 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"86\" height=\"18\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/2/462a59b3600aeddbc8084b61fbac286338e94da6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a-4) = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"88\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/6/b96aad980355edeb5064129abb0e4b4896832344.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(b-4) = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"86\" height=\"18\" />. This allows for 2 possibilities: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/2/372b122f51cad9f701b1d946b28c2f07f55c18de.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(5,12)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"51\" height=\"20\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/d/0bd97f1a6f1d76907ee5c4460c2f1fe587beb8d5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(6,8)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" /> which gives us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/8/ec89b8b00ff85a0cd6ff3bd4219acd2290c3c373.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B)} \\: 2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"55\" height=\"30\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_10B\" title=\"2008 AMC 10B\">2008 AMC 10B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_10B_Problems\" title=\"2008 AMC 10B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_10B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2008 AMC 10B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2008 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 22\">Problem 22</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2008 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 24\">Problem 24</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2008 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_2\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2008 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2008 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_4\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2008 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2008 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2008 AMC 10B P